WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:05.834
This example combines WHERE GROUP BY and HAVING in
one query The

00:00:05.861 --> 00:00:10.705
row-level rule keeps sales whose price is at least
twenty-five dollars Those

00:00:10.718 --> 00:00:16.258
qualifying rows are then grouped by category We
calculate total quantity and

00:00:16.284 --> 00:00:21.692
total revenue for each category Finally HAVING keeps
only groups whose total

00:00:21.705 --> 00:00:27.225
quantity is above the required threshold Before
running it predict

00:00:27.251 --> 00:00:32.017
whether every category will remain Then run the
query and compare the

00:00:32.030 --> 00:00:37.638
result Look carefully at the difference between the
price condition and the

00:00:37.651 --> 00:00:42.311
quantity condition Price belongs to each source row
so it is checked

00:00:42.338 --> 00:00:47.311
in WHERE Total quantity exists only after grouping
so it is checked

00:00:47.325 --> 00:00:52.604
in HAVING This is the full aggregation pattern you
will use frequently

00:00:52.630 --> 00:00:54.117
in real analytical work
